It is March, but it is still very cold in Berlin.
I am walking to the U-Bahn.
Today is an especially cold morning.
An icy wind is blowing through the streets.
Every morning I put on my jacket from Mexico.
That is a very thin jacket.
Today I am also wearing a thick sweater, because it is so cold.
The thick sweater is cozy, but it is not warm enough.
The cold wind just goes through the thin jacket.
I am freezing a lot on the short walk.
My colleagues often wear thick scarves and large hats.
I am not wearing a hat.
I have really had enough.
I need a real winter coat.
A good winter coat is very important in Berlin.
A warm coat perhaps costs a lot of money.
But I am buying a new coat this weekend.
